On Wed, 14 Oct 2026 16:48:22 -0700, Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com> wrote:
> I don't want to hide superseded either. Right now I'm just tagging
> items, so I can filter them out manually in notmuch.

Understood. The hiding patch is gone, and nothing is excluded by
default. "not tag:superseded" filters the old threads out.

> I really need a working superseded patch so that I can reduce the number
> of messages I have.

It is posted as "[PATCH v2 0/2] notmuch: Tag superseded series" [1].
It applies to b/dev@upstream on its own, without "[PATCH] notmuch:
Tag patches reported committed" [2]. Patch 1 tags threads that a
"Link to vN" line names. Patch 2 tags threads that a reply retires
with a closing Superseded-by trailer.

I ran it against a copy of the notmuch database here. Patch 1 tags 26
threads, 131 messages, and every one is an older version of a series.
After you apply it, one "notmuch new" tags them, because post-new
already runs mail-tag.sh. The seven threads that have no Link line,
listed in my earlier reply in this thread [3], stay untagged until
someone replies to each with a Superseded-by trailer.

"[PATCH 0/2] notmuch: Tag approved and rejected threads" [4] was
built on v1 and its doc patch still says superseded threads are
hidden. I will send a v2 of it on top of this series.

